My first wizard to ascend! Yay!

Normally I lean towards the school of thought which proclaims every 
character ascendable (not that I manage, but I like having 
principles..). This one on the other hand, had so unspectacular 
equipment (/oMake Invisible, +Cure Blindness, =FireRes and =+1Adornment) 
that I decided to check out the fountains - just in case.

And I got lucky on the first draught; wish for +0 [SDSM. From then on I 
was careful. Scrollshop on level 2 bought my starting spellbooks, and 
sold me a few other spellbooks instead (bought them back much later). A 
hill orc dropped speed boots. :)

Bones in Minetown had a +oDrainLife which I used to good effect on 
nymphs and in Sokoban where Forcebolt could be hard on luck. Did mine's 
end before Sokoban, though, which was the Catacombs: lots of nice 
spells. S gave me another reflection, but I'd found an "oESP which I 
used instead.

Quest started from the Rouge level (didn't know that was possible..).
Altar on level 18. Still only using a sack. At least it teaches me to 
take care with the inventory.. :( Wrote +Identify with the so far only 
marker found, before going on the quest. Splatted the Dark One with a 
Cream Pie before killing him - should I have lost alignment for this, 
due to disrespect? :D

An orc dropped a magic harp, and I found a standard one in the Minetown 
hardware store.

Cone of Cold for Medusa's level - oh how I love that spell...
Used the standard harp to open/close the castle door, used the /WoW for 
bag of holding, helm of brilliance and lots more markers. Used the magic 
harp on the castle dragons:
1 white
2 blue
1 gray

The white died in the Valley, then we went back up to raize the various 
temples (after getting all the protection I could out of them) and shops 
(not Izchak). I used the Quest as the Eye's starting base to get to my 
altar, and on Home 1 a polytrap turned one of the blues into an Aleax. 
At this point I decided to name my pets Indigo (blue D), Angelus (A) and 
Greywing (gray D). I accidentally killed Indigo once with an errant 
+Finger (bounced and I didn't know the ray would reach that far behind 
me), but revived and retamed him. After several messages of "Indigo is 
still eating" almost every time I went up and down stairs - and never 
for Greywing, I renamed Indigo to Glutton. Some might think they are 
just numbers and program objects - but I swear nethack pets have 
personalities...

Polypiled, guesswrote, and finally prayed to get all possible spells. 
Charm was almost the last, so I relied on the harp until then. Exchanged 
my original cloak for the robe of Moloch's priest in the Valley. Found 
another pair of speed boots in the castle armoury that I polyed into 
gauntlets of power. After that every spell exept Teleport Away (10%) was 
at 0 % failure.

On Juiblex' level a polytrap turned Angelus into an earth elemental - 
not sure what happened to it, but I kept it for quite a while.

I fell past Orcus' town and had to take him out without pets. Not a 
problem though. When I came back with my friends, Glutton played too 
long with a fire E, and then a clay or stone golem killed him. I'd grown 
so fond of him, I was stunned. In fact I was so stunned, I forgot all 
about reviving him, and so his corpse was left to rot. :'(

I finally found a black dragon almost at the bottom of Gehennon - it 
took out two temporary pets, but I managed to get Greywing with me back 
to stash to pick up a tinning kit. On the way down again I found a 
saddle, and mounted my dragon. To my great dismay both dragon and saddle 
were disintegrated by that damned black D. I had decided I didn't want 
to risk Greywing eating the corpse before me, so I dismounted before 
attacking, but I should of course just have killed it first, moved a 
little bit away, dismounted - and then come back to eat it.. :(

After that I only had a few temporary pets - two purple worms, a blue 
dragon and an Umber Hulk that I left for too long.

Rodney turned up in the Sanctum, but I fingered him and everything 
else that looked like it might be susceptible, and he was never a big 
deal.

The mysterious force was not so bad, and the run back up was 
unmemorable. Titans are susceptible to fingering, L, h and ; were 
genocided.

Polypiled and enchanted at my stashlevel to finally get a nice shirt. 
Reread a few spells. Picked up the crystal ball I'd found earlier. Earth 
was very short - only a single wand charge! Air required a !oFull 
Healing, and several /oTeleport charges. Fire and Water were more 
tedious than anything else.

Astral had pestilence to the left, famine in the middle and death to the 
right. I came through on the left so I tried that first. My hitpoints 
never suffered much, but charm, light and jump, mixed with the 
occasional teleport and finger, drew hard on the Power points. 
Pestilence guarded the Neutral altar, so I tried Famine. This was 
Lawful, so I donned my espescially treasured [HoOpposite Alignment, and 
offered the Amulet to Ptah.

